message: >-
  If you use DevRepro Doctor in research or engineering work, please cite it.
title: DevRepro Doctor
type: software
authors:
  - alias: webdevsamran
    name: "@webdevsamran"
    website: "https://github.com/webdevsamran"
repository-code: "https://github.com/webdevsamran/devrepro-doctor"
url: "https://github.com/webdevsamran/devrepro-doctor"
abstract: >-
  Cross-platform diagnostics, reproducibility auditing, machine-to-machine
  environment diffs, AI-agent readiness assessment and safe repair planning
  for developer machines, project toolchains, SDKs, containers and build
  dependencies. Determines why a given repository fails to build on a given
  machine, emits a pinned container that reproduces the failure, and reports
  whether an automated contributor can operate in the repository safely.
  Read-only by default, with no telemetry: every scan stays on the machine
  that produced it.
